      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So when do you lose your moderator badge? Do we have elections?<span></span></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Kinda - if enough people complain to GtG, I'm pretty sure I'll be given the boot.&nbsp; <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/blush.png?v=12\" title=\":blush:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":blush:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> </p>\n<p><span>Why? You looking for a bribe?&nbsp; <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/open_mouth.png?v=12\" title=\":open_mouth:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":open_mouth:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> </span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span>Seriously, in case there are folks wondering: GtG picks their Mods, and will add and remove folks as they deem it appropriate/necessary. If I'm not doing the job the way they want it done, I assume I'll be told my Mod privs will be taken away (as they should be).&nbsp;</span></p>",
